<http://data.silknow.org/object/65c5fd69-091a-3b02-96da-9f6fc3025729/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cross-stitch.  White linen; the design of conventional, symmetrical plant forms running from the outer edge, toward  the center, birds and animals, is worked with red, blue, black, yellow and green silk.  On three sides of the back are symmetrical conventional plant forms; on the fourth side a border of blocks.  The back and front are joined with fagoting, done with red and blue cotton.  There are silk tassels on two corners."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/65c5fd69-091a-3b02-96da-9f6fc3025729> .

<http://data.silknow.org/mfa>
        ecrm:P106_is_composed_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b929e865-56fe-314a-bf35-080405a80666> .

